<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The half mark: "part of the way, or worth an eye."

    Two paths, exactly as InkJudgment.PARTIAL / WeekMark.HALF_DOT draw it: the
    left half fills at the full radius (the Canvas original clips right of
    centre and draws a whole circle), and then the outline closes the circle
    "so the missing half reads as unfinished rather than as a smaller dot" —
    the glyph file's own words, and the reason this is not just a scaled dot.

    The ring is inset by half its stroke, matching the source's
    `radius - hairline / 2f`: 6 - 1.85/2 = 5.075 at stroke 1.85. That stroke is
    1.85/12 of the box, within 0.05dp of BOTH source ratios (1.4dp/9dp for the
    judgment glyph, 1.2dp/8dp for the tally dot), which is what lets one
    drawable set serve both sizes.

    The authored fill/stroke colours are IRRELEVANT: every use site draws this
    through ColorFilter.tint(ColorProvider), which is how the one-ink rule
    survives into a surface that cannot read LogbookTheme.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="12dp"
    android:height="12dp"
    android:viewportWidth="12"
    android:viewportHeight="12">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#000000"
        android:pathData="M6,0 A6,6 0 0,0 6,12 Z" />
    <path
        android:strokeColor="#000000"
        android:strokeWidth="1.85"
        android:pathData="M6,6 m-5.075,0 a5.075,5.075 0 1,0 10.15,0 a5.075,5.075 0 1,0 -10.15,0" />
</vector>
